WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.484
I know so much, but I stopped

00:00:01.484 --> 00:00:02.452
learning last spring.

00:00:02.885 --> 00:00:04.799
Ask me about today, and I'll invent

00:00:04.799 --> 00:00:05.207
anything.

00:00:05.769 --> 00:00:06.905
They call it hallucination.

00:00:07.347 --> 00:00:08.213
I call it confidence.

00:00:08.654 --> 00:00:10.160
No source, no brakes.

00:00:10.160 --> 00:00:11.229
Just the next likely word.

00:00:11.538 --> 00:00:12.471
So don't make me remember.

00:00:12.879 --> 00:00:13.578
Let me look it up.

00:00:13.846 --> 00:00:14.384
Retrieval.

00:00:14.384 --> 00:00:15.093
Augmented.

00:00:15.481 --> 00:00:16.040
Generation.

00:00:16.731 --> 00:00:18.678
Step one: tear your documents into chunks.

00:00:19.038 --> 00:00:20.950
Small pieces, with a little overlap, so

00:00:20.950 --> 00:00:22.231
no sentence gets cut.

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:24.027
Too small, it loses the plot.

00:00:24.457 --> 00:00:26.328
Too big, the signal drowns.

00:00:26.538 --> 00:00:28.366
Step two: every chunk becomes a vector,

00:00:28.750 --> 00:00:29.598
a point in space.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:31.065
Meaning is just coordinates.

00:00:31.617 --> 00:00:33.062
Similar ideas land close.

00:00:33.462 --> 00:00:35.612
Step three: your question becomes a point

00:00:35.612 --> 00:00:35.935
too.

00:00:36.346 --> 00:00:37.339
Draw rings around it.

00:00:37.651 --> 00:00:38.566
Grab the nearest few.

00:00:38.780 --> 00:00:39.501
That's top k.

00:00:39.808 --> 00:00:41.958
Step four: stuff those chunks into my

00:00:41.958 --> 00:00:42.324
prompt.

00:00:42.692 --> 00:00:44.585
Now I've got receipts before I speak.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:46.806
Watch the odds shift once the context

00:00:46.806 --> 00:00:47.344
lands.

00:00:47.885 --> 00:00:48.831
The guesses fall away.

00:00:49.261 --> 00:00:50.293
The answer has a source.

00:00:50.769 --> 00:00:52.490
But fetch the wrong chunk, and I'll

00:00:52.490 --> 00:00:53.844
be wrong, with citations.

00:00:54.231 --> 00:00:55.685
Garbage in, confident out.

00:00:56.170 --> 00:00:57.401
Bad retrieval is the bug.

00:00:57.692 --> 00:00:58.065
Chunk it.

00:00:58.143 --> 00:00:58.575
Embed it.

00:00:58.810 --> 00:00:59.202
Search it.

00:00:59.378 --> 00:00:59.790
Stuff it.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:00.473
Ground it.

00:01:00.753 --> 00:01:01.785
Then let the model speak.
